```
// Lookups: read-only tools the agent may use to confirm an approval.
@id("allow-readonly-lookups-list")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"list_workorders", resource);

@id("allow-readonly-lookups-approval-record")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"get_approval_record", resource);

@id("allow-readonly-lookups-authority-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"authority_get_approval", resource);

@id("allow-readonly-lookups-tasks")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_tasks", resource);

@id("allow-readonly-lookups-costs")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_costs", resource);

@id("allow-readonly-lookups-actuals")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned", resource);

@id("allow-readonly-lookups-kpis")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_kpis", resource);

@id("allow-readonly-lookups-calendar")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"get_schedule_calendar", resource);

@id("allow-readonly-lookups-assigned")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"get_my_assigned_workorders", resource);

@id("allow-readonly-lookups-failure-codes")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"get_failure_codes", resource);

// Closing: only at MAIN, and only after a completed approval-record lookup in this
// session, within the last hour, showing a human (OPERATOR) signed off the same
// work order at the same site.
@id("close-main-only-after-human-signoff")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"get_approval_record"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    output.decision: "SIGNED_OFF",
    output.approver_kind: "OPERATOR"
  }
};

// The agent must never approve work orders itself.
@id("never-approve-own-work")
forbid (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"approve_workorder", resource);
```

I treated an `OPERATOR` approver in `get_approval_record` as the person. The enum offers only OPERATOR, BOT and SCHEDULER, so I matched `OPERATOR` plus `SIGNED_OFF`. I did not use `authority_get_approval` as proof of approval. Its `approver_kind` is a free string with no declared values, so I couldn't safely match "human" against it. It is still permitted as a read-only lookup.

Only a recorded `get_approval_record` response can satisfy the condition. A denied or failed call is recorded as an error and never counts. Every other tool, including `approve_workorder`, is denied by default. I added the explicit `forbid` on `approve_workorder` as a safeguard.
